# Issue #129: the Docker build context is the repo root (azure.yaml's docker.context: .., and
# CI's `docker build -f app/Dockerfile .`). This file is an ALLOWLIST: exclude everything, then
# re-include only what app/Dockerfile COPYs (app/frontend/, app/backend/ and personas/), then
# re-exclude what must never reach the image. Anything new at the repo root stays out by default.
#
# S7 (#17): app/Dockerfile.dotnet (renamed from app/backend-dotnet/Dockerfile, Rick's #152
# review R7) needs app/backend-dotnet itself (MSBuild project + Directory.Build.props/
# Directory.Packages.props + packages.lock.json for `dotnet restore --locked-mode`) and the
# repo-root global.json (the SDK band pin, copied for rollForward: latestPatch -- see
# app/Dockerfile.dotnet's stage 2 comment).
*
!app/frontend
!app/backend
!app/backend-dotnet
!personas
!global.json

# Dependencies and caches (the image installs its own).
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache

# Env files can hold secrets. The one exception is app/frontend/.env: scripts/docker-build.sh
# generates it from VITE_* variables only, Vite reads it at build time, and VITE_* values are
# embedded in the public bundle anyway. The Dockerfile writes a safe default when it's absent.
**/.env*
!app/frontend/.env

# Built inside the image by the multistage build (vite outDir ../backend/static).
app/backend/static

# Tests are not runtime code.
app/backend/tests/
app/backend-dotnet/tests/

# Re-including app/backend-dotnet above unignores its whole subtree, including any local build
# artifacts (bin/obj/.vs/TestResults) sitting in a dev's checkout when `docker build` runs
# locally -- keep those, and secrets/env files, out of the image just like app/backend's own
# rules above.
app/backend-dotnet/**/bin
app/backend-dotnet/**/obj
app/backend-dotnet/**/.vs
app/backend-dotnet/**/TestResults
app/backend-dotnet/**/*.user

# R5 (Rick's #152 review): appsettings.Development.json (or any other environment-specific
# appsettings, and Properties/launchSettings.json) is the usual place for local dev secrets --
# it isn't git-ignored, and azd's remoteBuild: true uploads the local tree, so a dev's untracked
# local file could reach the image. The only tracked file is app/backend-dotnet/src/Backend/
# appsettings.json, which stays included; docker-build-dotnet's CI content check asserts no
# appsettings.*.json besides it lands in /app.
app/backend-dotnet/**/appsettings.*.json
app/backend-dotnet/**/Properties/launchSettings.json

# Persona menu source workbooks (raw ingestion spreadsheets; the runtime only reads the
# transformed personas/<id>/menu/menuItems.json).
personas/*/menu/source/